@startuml
title E06 - Trusted time and boundary handling
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
participant "Authenticated time source" as Clock
control "S01\nShared contracts" as S01
control "H07\nHub lifecycle/config" as H07
control "H03\nHub time" as H03
control "H05\nHub rules adapter" as H05
control "S02\nDeterministic rules core" as S02
control "H02\nHub persistence" as H02
Clock -> S01: Authenticated wall-time anchor + uncertainty
S01 -> H03: Validated time-anchor contract
H07 -> H03: Apply timezone/window configuration version
H03 -> H03: Estimate earliest/latest wall time from monotonic elapsed time
H03 -> H05: Return trust state and uncertainty bounds
H05 -> S02: Check event-window overlap or grace deadline eligibility
S02 --> H05: Return deterministic evidence/incident/suppression result
H05 -> H02: Persist decision reason and stable window ID
note over H03,H05: No anchor, monotonic rollback, excessive uncertainty or >72-hour expiry suppresses absence decisions.
note over Clock,H02: Outcome - Routine decisions use bounded trusted time and remain deterministic across reboot, drift and boundary ambiguity.
@enduml
